    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Cso4WAZSWbQutHMvcAniFJ)_\n\n## What\n\nTidy of the Emacs `CHANGELOG.org` for the PRs merged since last night (#275, #276, #278, #280 to #283), plus the new root changelog.\n\n- **Stale lines back**: the union merge of older branches had brought back lines the last tidy had already removed (\"Tangle check red on main\", \"Vault performance\", the old \"Emacs hangs at start (open #267)\"). I removed them again and put the single \"Emacs hangs at start\" line back (all its PRs are merged, the cause is still unconfirmed).\n- **Being developed**: the three keymap lines (#278, #283, #284) are one; new line for #285 (open); the Stow lines are gone because every PR in the move is merged.\n- **Author and literature note lint**: one line each for #280, #281, #282.\n- **Reviewing and merging in Magit**: one line each for #272 and #275 (the Stow work on the Emacs side). Their detail is in the \"Changes by pull request\" sections of `sp-vcontrol` and `sp-globals`.\n- **New root `CHANGELOG.org`**: following the new rule that non-Emacs changes go there, it starts with the \"Moving from yadm to Stow\" set (#271, #274).\n\n## Left out on purpose\n\n- #284 and #285 are open and add their own lines when they merge.\n- #276 and #279 are doc-only / the previous tidy.\n- #255 (beets) and #225 (iPod) merged before the new rule; say if you want them in the root changelog.\n\nOnly prose changed, no code blocks, so the `tangle` check should be unaffected.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAhURtzPFib2Qr56NG)_",
